# Open Design Local Development & Daemon Orchestration

## When to Use
Use this skill whenever the user asks to:
- Start, restart, or verify the local **Open Design Local** environment (`../DNK_Vibe/Open Design Local`).
- Modify or debug UI components (`apps/web/src/components/...`) or daemon integrations (`apps/daemon/src/...`) in Open Design Local.
- Configure or inspect Google Cloud / Vertex AI models (`/api/gcloud/models`, `/api/gcloud/status`) inside Open Design.

## Architecture & Port Mapping
Open Design Local operates as a split local-first architecture:
1. **Daemon (`@open-design/daemon`)**: Local Express + SQLite (`better-sqlite3`) + plugin registry server. Listens on `OD_PORT` (configured as `127.0.0.1:54301` in DNK workflows, default `7456`).
2. **Web UI (`@open-design/web`)**: Next.js 16 (Turbopack) frontend served on port `54330`. Reads `OD_PORT` at runtime (`next.config.ts`) to proxy `/api/*`, `/artifacts/*`, and `/frames/*` requests directly to `http://127.0.0.1:${OD_PORT}`.

## Numbered Workflow: Starting Open Design Locally

### 0. Canonical Port Registry Check (`core/registry/port_registry.yaml`)
Open Design Local is registered in `core/registry/port_registry.yaml` (ADR-092) with dedicated ports `54301` (Daemon) and `54330` (Web UI). Never launch it on default ports `7456` or `3000`.

### 1. Preferred Unified Launcher (`pnpm start` / `tools-dev`)
The root `package.json` in `../DNK_Vibe/Open Design Local` includes pinned scripts using `@open-design/tools-dev`:
```bash
cd "../DNK_Vibe/Open Design Local"
pnpm start   # runs: pnpm exec tools-dev start web --daemon-port 54301 --web-port 54330
pnpm status  # checks running sidecars
pnpm stop    # stops web & daemon cleanly
```
`tools-dev start web --daemon-port 54301 --web-port 54330` automatically verifies Node v24, rebuilds `@open-design/daemon` if source files in `apps/daemon/src` are newer than `dist/cli.js`, passes `OD_WEB_PORT=54330` for CORS trust, and starts Next.js on `127.0.0.1:54330` proxied to `127.0.0.1:54301`.

### 2. Check Running Processes & Listeners
Before spawning new instances manually, check if the daemon (`54301`) or web server (`54330`) are already listening:
```bash
lsof -i :54330 -i :54301
```

### 2. Start the Daemon with Node v24 and OD_WEB_PORT
The project enforces `"node": "~24"` in `package.json`, and `better-sqlite3` native bindings are compiled against Node v24 ABI.
Additionally, the daemon strictly validates browser origins via `allowedBrowserPorts()` in `origin-validation.ts`. When running the Next.js frontend on port `54330`, pass `OD_WEB_PORT=54330` so mutating requests (`POST /api/gcloud/login`, etc.) are not blocked with `403 Cross-origin requests are not allowed`.
- **Pitfall**: On macOS with Homebrew, the default `node` in `$PATH` (`/opt/homebrew/bin/node`) may point to Node v25+, which causes `ERR_DLOPEN_FAILED` when loading `better-sqlite3.node`.
- **Fix**: Explicitly invoke `/usr/local/bin/node` (Node v24.x) with both `OD_PORT` and `OD_WEB_PORT`:
```bash
OD_PORT=54301 OD_WEB_PORT=54330 /usr/local/bin/node "../DNK_Vibe/Open Design Local/apps/daemon/dist/cli.js" --no-open
```
*(Run with `background=true` in the `terminal` tool and poll after ~2s to confirm `[od] listening on http://127.0.0.1:54301`.)*

### 3. Start the Next.js Web Dev Server Coupled to `OD_PORT`
Launch the Next.js dev server with `OD_PORT=54301` (or `DAEMON_ORIGIN="http://127.0.0.1:54301"`) so its internal rewrite proxy routes `/api/*` calls to the active daemon.
- **Pitfall (`pnpm run dev -- -p 54330`)**: With `pnpm`, passing `-- -p 54330` appends a literal `--` to `next dev --turbopack -- -p 54330`, causing Next.js 16 to treat `-p` as a project directory path and crash with `Invalid project directory provided, no such directory: .../apps/web/-p`.
- **Fix**: Invoke `npx next dev` directly (or pass args without `--` in pnpm):
```bash
cd "../DNK_Vibe/Open Design Local/apps/web" && OD_PORT=54301 DAEMON_ORIGIN="http://127.0.0.1:54301" PORT=54330 npx next dev --turbopack -p 54330 -H 127.0.0.1
```
*(Run with `background=true` and poll until port `54330` is listening and returns `HTTP/1.1 200 OK`.)*

### 4. Build Commands (After Code Edits)
- **Rebuild Daemon** (required after editing `apps/daemon/src/**` since the daemon runs compiled `dist/cli.js`):
  ```bash
  pnpm --dir "../DNK_Vibe/Open Design Local/apps/daemon" run build
  ```
- **Rebuild Web** (to verify production static/server bundle integrity):
  ```bash
  NODE_OPTIONS="--max-old-space-size=8192" pnpm --dir "../DNK_Vibe/Open Design Local/apps/web" run build
  ```

### 5. Upstream Delta Sync & Unified Runtime Linking (`~/.dnk_runtime`)
When syncing `../DNK_Vibe/Open Design Local` with upstream `https://github.com/nexu-io/open-design` (`origin/main`):
1. **Backup DNK Customizations First**: Never discard or overwrite the 45+ custom DNK files (`gcloud-provider.ts`, `routes/gcloud.ts`, `byok-opencode.ts`, `font-recovery.ts`, `ModelsSection.tsx`, `SettingsDialog.tsx`). Commit all working-tree changes to `dnk-custom-backup` before fetching upstream:
   ```bash
   cd "../DNK_Vibe/Open Design Local"
   git checkout -b dnk-custom-backup
   git add -A && git commit -m "chore(backup): preserve dnk vertex and ui customizations"
   git fetch origin main
   git checkout main
   git reset --hard origin/main
   git cherry-pick dnk-custom-backup
   ```
2. **Centralized Virtual Store Linking (Zero-Bloat Invariant)**:
   Never allow physical `.pnpm` stores (~2.4 GB) inside `Open Design Local/node_modules`. Link dependencies to `~/.dnk_runtime/pnpm_virtual_store` (~560 KB footprint):
   ```bash
   rm -rf node_modules apps/*/node_modules packages/*/node_modules
   pnpm install --virtual-store-dir ~/.dnk_runtime/pnpm_virtual_store
   ```
3. **`packages/dsh-runtime` Postinstall `commander` v15 Type Mismatch**:
   During `pnpm install`, `postinstall.mjs` compiles `packages/dsh-runtime`. When `commander@15.0.0` is resolved against `@deepseek-ai/dsh-cmdline` (typed for `commander@4`), `src/startup.ts(37,21)` fails with `TS2740`. Cast `parseCmdline(ctx, program as any)` in `packages/dsh-runtime/src/startup.ts`.

## Verification Steps
Always verify both the frontend HTTP response and the daemon proxy pass-through before reporting completion:
```bash
curl -sI http://127.0.0.1:54330/ | head -n 5
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:54330/api/gcloud/models
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:54330/api/gcloud/status
```
- `http://127.0.0.1:54330/` must return `HTTP/1.1 200 OK`.
- `/api/gcloud/models` must return the JSON list of Vertex AI / Gemini models proxied from the daemon (`54301`).
- `/api/agents` must return `"id": "byok-opencode", "available": true`. If `"available": false` or `"executablePath": null`, UI prompts will fail instantly with `"Запуск не вдався" / "Не вдалося завершити завдання"`.
- Stream verification via OpenAI Proxy with Vertex AI:
  ```bash
  curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:54301/api/proxy/openai/stream \
    -H "Origin: http://127.0.0.1:54330" \
    -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
    -d '{"baseUrl":"https://aiplatform.googleapis.com","apiKey":"CONNECTED_VIA_GCLOUD","model":"google/gemini-4-argon","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"Hi"}]}' | head -n 15
  ```
  Must stream `event: delta` SSE chunks with real model generation output and complete with `event: end`.

## Pitfalls & Guardrails
- **`mergeProviderModelOptions` TypeError (`Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'trim')`)**:
  The frontend settings dialog (`SettingsDialog.tsx` -> `providerModelsCache.ts`) expects `/api/provider/models` to return objects conforming to `ProviderModelOption` (`{ id: string; label: string }`) with `kind: 'success'`. If `apps/daemon/src/integrations/provider-models.ts` returns `{ id, name }` instead of `{ id, label }` for Vertex AI models, `model.label.trim()` throws a fatal Next.js Runtime TypeError on `/settings`. Always return `{ id: m.id, label: m.label }` with `kind: 'success'` in `provider-models.ts`, and defensively guard `(model?.label ?? model?.name ?? '').trim()` in `providerModelsCache.ts`.
- **Vertex AI OpenAPI Path Normalization in Chat Proxy (`/api/proxy/openai/stream`)**:
  When configuring Open Design chat with Vertex AI (`baseUrl: "https://aiplatform.googleapis.com"`), `appendVersionedApiPath` default behavior transforms `https://aiplatform.googleapis.com` into `https://aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1/chat/completions`, which 404s. The daemon must intercept `aiplatform.googleapis.com` in `apps/daemon/src/routes/chat.ts` and rewrite the endpoint using `buildVertexBaseUrl()` (`/v1beta1/projects/{project}/locations/global/endpoints/openapi/chat/completions`). Additionally, Bearer access tokens from `gcloud auth print-access-token` must be resolved via `refreshVertexTokenAsync()` whenever `apiKey === 'CONNECTED_VIA_GCLOUD'`.
- **`byok-opencode` "Запуск не вдався" / "opencode-cli not found in PATH"**:
  Open Design Web checks agent availability before dispatching BYOK tasks (`ProjectView.tsx`), and the daemon's execution runner (`resolveAgentLaunch` -> `resolveAmrOpenCodeExecutable`) resolves the binary at run time.
  - **CRITICAL ESM Pitfall**: `apps/daemon/package.json` uses `"type": "module"` (ESM). NEVER use CommonJS `__dirname` in `apps/daemon/src/runtimes/executables.ts` — TypeScript compiles it without error, but Node v24 throws `ReferenceError: __dirname is not defined` at runtime when spawning the agent! Always resolve relative to the pre-defined `RUNTIME_PROJECT_ROOT` constant (`path.resolve(RUNTIME_PROJECT_ROOT, 'node_modules/.pnpm/...')`).
  - Ensure `resolveAmrOpenCodeExecutable` in `apps/daemon/src/runtimes/executables.ts` resolves the bundled binary (`@powerformer/vela-cli-darwin-arm64/bin/libexec/opencode/opencode`) via `RUNTIME_PROJECT_ROOT`, and verify with an actual CLI spawn test before declaring completion.
- **`ERR_DLOPEN_FAILED` on `better-sqlite3`**: Never recompile native modules for Node v25 if `/usr/local/bin/node` (v24) is present; simply run the daemon with `/usr/local/bin/node`.
- **`403 Cross-origin requests are not allowed`**: Occurs if `OD_WEB_PORT=54330` is not provided to the daemon process or if port 54330 is omitted from `allowedBrowserPorts()` in `origin-validation.ts`. See `references/vertex_opencode_cors_integration.md`.
- **OpenCode Vertex AI Auth Failure (`AGENT_AUTH_REQUIRED` / «Вхід у OpenAI API via OpenCode не виконано»)**:
  - **Root Cause**: The `byok-opencode` agent runtime classifies any HTTP 401/403 from the provider as `AGENT_AUTH_REQUIRED` with the fixed label *"OpenAI API via OpenCode"*. Using `@ai-sdk/google` against Vertex AI (`aiplatform.googleapis.com`) fails with HTTP 401 (`API keys are not supported by this API. Expected OAuth2 access token...`) because `@ai-sdk/google` unconditionally injects the `x-goog-api-key` header whenever `apiKey` is provided, and throws `AI_LoadAPIKeyError` before the request if `apiKey` is omitted. Furthermore, the bundled `opencode` binary's internal `google-vertex` custom loader checks Application Default Credentials (ADC) files (`GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` / `application_default_credentials.json`) and ignores raw `gcloud` CLI OAuth tokens.
  - **Fix**: Route Vertex AI Gemini models in `apps/daemon/src/runtimes/byok-opencode.ts` via `npm: '@ai-sdk/openai-compatible'` pointing to Vertex AI's OpenAPI endpoint (`buildVertexBaseUrl()` -> `https://aiplatform.googleapis.com/v1beta1/projects/{project}/locations/global/endpoints/openapi`) with `apiKey: "{env:OPEN_DESIGN_BYOK_API_KEY}"` set to `getCachedToken()` and model IDs prefixed with `google/` (e.g., `google/gemini-4-argon`). Explicitly set `headers: { Authorization: "Bearer {env:OPEN_DESIGN_BYOK_API_KEY}" }` in provider config and export `OPEN_DESIGN_BYOK_API_KEY` into child spawn env.
- **HTTP 429 Rate Limit Misinterpretation (`AI_APICallError: Too Many Requests`)**:
  - **Root Cause**: In `apps/daemon/src/runtimes/opencode-log.ts`, `extractOpenCodeServiceFailure` fell back to `AGENT_AUTH_REQUIRED` for unparsed error strings. When Vertex AI returned HTTP 429 for high-demand models (like `gemini-4-argon`), OpenCode logged `AI_APICallError: Too Many Requests`, which was falsely surfaced to the user as a login failure.
  - **Fix**: Explicitly match `Too Many Requests` and rate limit strings to `RATE_LIMITED` (429). In `apps/daemon/src/routes/runs.ts`, provide automatic Vertex AI provider synthesis whenever `agentId === 'byok-opencode'` and the request lacks `byokProvider`. See `references/vertex_opencode_cors_integration.md`.
- **`Model not found: open-design-byok/default` & Hardcoded `DEFAULT_VERTEX_PROJECT` Billing Mismatch**:
  - **Root Cause 1**: In `apps/web/src/components/ModelsSection.tsx`, selecting a Vertex AI model updates `agentModels.opencode`, `gemini`, `claude`, and `codex`, but omits `agentModels['byok-opencode']`. Because `defaultAgentId` is `'byok-opencode'`, `cfg.model` remains unset or `'default'`, causing `apps/daemon/src/runtimes/byok-opencode.ts` to pass `-m open-design-byok/default` to `opencode run`, which fails immediately at 1s.
  - **Root Cause 2**: `apps/daemon/src/integrations/gcloud-provider.ts` hardcodes `DEFAULT_VERTEX_PROJECT` to a legacy project ID where billing may be disabled, ignoring the active billing-enabled GCP project (`project-be4f9ef3-582e-4567-a6d`).
  - **Fix**: Synchronize `agentModels['byok-opencode']` in `ModelsSection.tsx`, normalize `'default'` or empty model IDs to `'google/gemini-2.5-flash'` in `byok-opencode.ts`, and resolve the active billing-enabled GCP project in `gcloud-provider.ts`.
- **Unstyled HTML in Settings/Models**: Always use scoped CSS modules (`*.module.css`) referencing Open Design's native CSS tokens (`--bg-surface`, `--border-subtle`, `--accent`, `--text-primary`, `--text-secondary`) rather than unstyled raw HTML elements.
- **Secret Hygiene**: Never log or render raw GCloud Bearer tokens in full; mask tokens in UI previews and session logs.
- **Clean-Room Canvas & Semantic Drop Patterns (`morluto/rea` vs `dnk-web-design`)**: For clean-room reverse-engineering of live DOM artboards (`data-dnk-node-id` + `elementFromPoint`), semantic flex/margin drop placement (`computeDropPlacement`), and two-tier AST/Liquid write-back without `opencode` daemon bloat, see `references/rea_clean_room_canvas_patterns.md`.
